# Component Patterns

## Props

❌ BAD - no types, destructure everywhere:
function Button(props) {
  return <Pressable onPress={props.onPress}>{props.children}</Pressable>;
}

✅ GOOD - typed props interface:
interface ButtonProps {
  onPress: () => void;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}
const Button: React.FC<ButtonProps> = ({ onPress, children }) => { ... }

## Inline Functions

❌ BAD - new function every render:
<Pressable onPress={() => handlePress(item.id)}>

✅ GOOD - memoized callback:
const handleItemPress = useCallback(() => handlePress(item.id), [item.id]);
<Pressable onPress={handleItemPress}>

## Giant JSX

❌ BAD - 100+ lines of JSX in one component:
return (
  <View>
    <View><Text>...</Text><Image />...</View>
    <View><Text>...</Text><Image />...</View>
    // 80 more lines
  </View>
);

✅ GOOD - extract subcomponents:
return (
  <View>
    <AuthHeader />
    <AuthForm onSubmit={handleSubmit} />
    <AuthFooter />
  </View>
);

## Animations

❌ BAD - using old Animated API:
import { Animated } from 'react-native';
const fadeAnim = useRef(new Animated.Value(0)).current;

✅ GOOD - Reanimated on UI thread:
import Animated, { useSharedValue, useAnimatedStyle } from 'react-native-reanimated';
const opacity = useSharedValue(0);
